<section class="hero business-owner-hero"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">BUSINESS OWNERS</div><h1>You built the business intentionally.<span class="business-hero-gold ripl-gold">Your personal wealth deserves the same treatment.</span></h1><p class="lead">Business owners are often excellent capital allocators inside the company. The personal side can be a different story.</p><p class="lead">Your business gives you control over your income. Your investment business gives you control over your future.</p><div class="page-actions"><a class="btn" href="/contact/">Talk to the Team</a><a class="text-link" href="/assessment/?track=owner">Take the Quiz →</a></div></div></section>

<section class="owner-clarity"><div class="wrap owner-clarity-grid"><div class="ripl-photo-frame"><div class="photo-frame-image"><img src="/images/chase-team-office.png" alt="Chase Bellefeuille, Managing Partner at RIPL" width="1122" height="1402" loading="lazy"/></div></div><blockquote><p>“We believe successful people make excellent decisions when they can see their options with clarity.”</p><cite>Chase Bellefeuille · Managing Partner</cite></blockquote></div></section>

<section class="section finance-company"><div class="wrap"><div class="finance-company-intro finance-company-intro-grid"><div><div class="eyebrow">YOUR NEXT COMPANY DOESN’T NEED ANOTHER EMPLOYEE.</div><h2>Build your investment business.<br><span class="business-hero-gold">Put your lazy money to work.</span></h2><p class="lead">You know how to build a business that makes money. Now let’s give some of that money a job outside the business.</p><p>Think of it as a business of its own: a dedicated investment strategy funded with capital you can put to work after your operating needs, reserves and tax obligations are accounted for. We help you organize it, invest it with purpose and keep it connected to the life you want to build.</p></div><div class="finance-flow-slot"><FinanceCompanyFlow /></div></div><div class="finance-company-benefits"><article><span aria-hidden="true">0</span><h3>Employees to hire.</h3><p>No recruiting, staffing or payroll to manage.</p></article><article><span aria-hidden="true">0</span><h3>Operating business to run.</h3><p>No new location, inventory or customer pipeline to build.</p></article><article><span aria-hidden="true">1</span><h3>Clear plan for your money.</h3><p>Build wealth outside the company you already work hard to run.</p></article></div><p class="small finance-company-note">“Investment business” describes our planning approach, rather than a required new legal entity. There is no additional operating business overhead; investment and advisory costs still apply.</p><div class="finance-company-sale"><div><div class="eyebrow">BUILD WEALTH ALONG THE WAY.</div><h3>Selling your business should be<br><span class="business-hero-gold">the cherry on top.</span><span class="finance-company-mountain">Not the top of the mountain.</span></h3></div><div><p>What if a future sale added to the financial life you’ve already built, instead of being the event you’re counting on to make it all work?</p><p>That’s the goal. Keep building a strong business while deliberately growing wealth outside it. A sale can then create more options, rather than carry the whole plan.</p><p>We start by identifying what is genuinely available to invest, where it belongs and when you may need it. Your tax strategist helps confirm the tax and ownership implications before money moves. Your investment plan reflects your goals, time horizon and willingness to take risk.</p><a class="btn" href="/contact/">Talk to the Team</a><p class="small">Investments can lose value. Growth and a future business sale are not guaranteed.</p></div></div></div></section>

